# MIDI ingest

When the user attaches or points at `.mid` file(s) to add a song, **run the
script**. Do not hand-transcribe notes. Ignore this rule on unrelated work.

```bash
npm run ingest-midi -- \
  --id slug-here \
  --title "Song Title" \
  --subtitle "Version A · optional context" \
  --file path/to/arrangement.mid \
  --source-url "https://listing-page" \
  --source-file "original name.mid" \
  --source-file-url "https://…/original%20name.mid" \
  --collection "Site · Collection"
```

Split parts: `--voice` / `--chords` / `--bass` instead of `--file`. Flags:
`--id` `--title` required. `--source-url` and original `--source-file` are
required for anything we download or are handed. Also pass `--source-file-url`
when the `.mid` has its own URL. Paths may be absolute.

**Duplicates:** same listing title + **different filename/URL** → ingest both.
New `--id`, name the version in `--title` / `--subtitle` (Version A / B).
Same `.mid` listed twice (same filename or file URL already in catalog) →
**skip**. The script exits if `origin.filename` / `origin.fileUrl` matches.
Do not invent a second copy of the same file.

**Category labels:** `yesterday-*` → pop/rock/folk. Jewish/Yiddish/klezmer
repertoire → `KLEZMER_LABELS`. Blues (MidKar, pdmusic.org) → `BLUES_LABELS`.
Other FreeSheetMusic pages get their own set (e.g. irish/celtic/folk) — do
not stamp klezmer labels on a jig from `/irish`.

## After the script

1. Writes `public/midi/<id>/`, compact `public/catalog/<id>.json` (includes
   `meta.origin`, labels, subtitle), and appends a row to
   `src/lib/songs/manifest.json`. Do not generate a per-song `.ts` module.
2. Never overwrite an existing `--id` unless the user asks to re-ingest.
3. Update the MidiLab Song Library blurb. `npx tsc --noEmit`.
4. Do not commit unless asked. Do not say it is live.

## What the pipeline keeps / drops

- Parser: `src/lib/song/fromMidi.ts`. The roll **fetches**
  `/catalog/<id>.json` on select, expands it, then runs
  `documentToRollView`. It does not re-parse `.mid` and does not import
  catalog JSON into the TypeScript graph. The picker reads
  `manifest.json` only.
- First tempo + first time signature only (tempo maps flatten to one BPM).
- Quantize 0.5 beat; skip GM drum channel 9.
- **Keep lyrics.** MIDI `lyrics` meta and KAR `text` events become
  `document.lyrics` (timed). Companion `.txt` sheets use `--lyric-sheet`
  → `document.lyricSheet`. Do not drop a `.kar` just because it has words.
- `songBars()` uses quarter-beats per bar (`num * 4 / den`), so 6/8 is 3
  quarters, not 6. Unknown meters (e.g. 3/8) still load; the Meter dropdown
  prepends them.
- Prefer public-domain / traditional / user-owned files. Still ingest locally
  if asked, but say that is not clearance to ship on instrumaps.com.

## FreeSheetMusic.net (library seed)

Hub: [Worldfolk](https://www.freesheetmusic.net/music/worldfolk/). Listings
are `Midi | Pdf | title` with `.mid` next to the HTML page.

**Already ingested (do not repeat):**
[Klezmer Folktunes](https://www.freesheetmusic.net/music/worldfolk/klezmer.html)
(~128 unique files, 2026-08-30). Re-run `npm run ingest-klezmer-page` only to
pick up *new* filenames; known `origin.filename` / `fileUrl` are skipped.
Three listing links were HTML, not MIDI (`roumanian hora & bulgar`,
`sonya & anoushka`, the long *Nacht in Gan Eydn* English title).

**Explore next** — same site, other pages, same ingest rules (source URL +
original filename; both versions if the files differ). Worldfolk siblings:
`/music/worldfolk/{belgian,celtic,around-the-world,popular,guitar,irish,russian,scottish}`.
Also `/music/{bach,beethoven,christmas,oneills,…}`. Only tag
`jewish/klezmer/yiddish` when the repertoire actually is that; Irish/Scottish
etc. need their own labels. Use `scripts/ingest-listing-page.ts` (`--preset`)
for new listing pages rather than copy-pasting a script per page.

## Blues listings (local catalog)

`npm run ingest-listing-page -- --preset blues` (or `midkar-old` /
`midkar-chicago` / `pdmusic-blues`). Known `origin.filename` / `fileUrl`
are skipped. MidKar needs a browser User-Agent. MidKar is **not** clearance
to ship on instrumaps.com.

**Already ingested (2026-09-05):**
- [MidKar old blues](https://midkar.com/Blues/Blues_MIDIs.html) (~380)
- [Wayne's Blues Venue · Chicago/Delta/Texas](https://midkar.com/Blues/Chicago/Chicago.html) (~264)
- [pdmusic.org Blues](https://dirkncl.github.io/pdmusic_org/blues.html) (~28; lyric sheets when present)

Do not re-ingest those filenames. Wayne's other venue categories
(Classic Rock, BTO-only, Motown, …) are not in yet.
